<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins contracts worth 200 mln skr.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins contracts worth 200 mln skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB said on Thursday that it had signed three strategic contracts with Swedish state-owned telecom operator Telia worth 200 million crowns.  </p>
<p>Ericsson said in a statement that it would supply public telecom switching equipment to Telia's markets in the Nordic region and upgrade AXE exchange stations.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
